 # Usability and accessibility evaluation (area 3)
 
 ## Run the tests (PowerShell)
+Run these commands from the repository root. Create the evidence directories first:
 ```
+New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force docs/evidence/e2e/screens | Out-Null
+New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force docs/evidence/accessibility/before | Out-Null
+New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force docs/evidence/lighthouse/before | Out-Null
 python -m pip install -r requirements-e2e.txt
 python -m playwright install chromium
 python -m pytest tests/team/e2e -v --junitxml=docs/evidence/e2e/junit.xml
 ```
-`E2E_SHOTS=1` (set `$env:E2E_SHOTS="1"` first) saves screenshots to `docs/evidence/e2e/screens/`. Failed tests save a screenshot automatically. The browser tests are skipped when Playwright is not installed.
+Set `$env:E2E_SHOTS="1"` before pytest to save step screenshots to `docs/evidence/e2e/screens/`. Failed tests save a screenshot automatically. If Playwright is not installed, the E2E test modules are excluded from collection; install `requirements-e2e.txt` and Chromium before treating the E2E suite as executed.
 
 ## axe-core (before)
 ```
+New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force docs/evidence/accessibility/before | Out-Null
 $env:A11Y_LABEL="before"; python -m pytest tests/team/e2e/test_e2e_accessibility.py -s
 ```
-Reports: `docs/evidence/accessibility/before/*.json`. The test uses `axe-playwright-python` (the same axe-core engine as `@axe-core/playwright`). If your marker insists on the npm package, say so in the report or ask the TA.
+Reports: `docs/evidence/accessibility/before/*.json`. The test uses the Python `axe-playwright-python` wrapper around axe-core. Do not describe it as the npm `@axe-core/playwright` package; if the marker specifically requires that npm package, confirm acceptability with the TA.
 
 ## Lighthouse (before)
 Needs Node. In one window `python scripts/e2e_server.py`; in another:
